I stand on the platform.
I am waiting for the U-Bahn.
After a few minutes, the train arrives.
The U-Bahn is bright yellow.
The train stops.
The doors open.
First, the people get out.
Then I get in.
I have to travel far today.
A loud beep warns us.
The doors close.
The train pulls away.
We roll into the dark tunnel.
I travel by U-Bahn every day.
The carriage is not very full today.
I look for a free seat.
A seat by the window is still free.
I sit down.
I hold my backpack on my lap.
